    answer: 'Friday is the best day of the week: Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet said the best day on which the sun has risen is Friday, on which Adam was created (Sahih Muslim 854).\n\nWhat is taught for Friday:\n- Wash (ghusl) and go early. Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet said whoever bathes on Friday like the bath of janabah and goes early to the prayer, it is as if he offered a camel in sacrifice, and the reward lessens for each later hour (Sahih al-Bukhari 881).\n- Clean your teeth with the siwak and wear perfume if you have it: Sahih al-Bukhari 880. (The scholars differ on whether the bath itself is obligatory or strongly recommended.)\n- Go to the prayer when the adhan is called and leave trade for it: "when [the adhan] is called for the prayer on the day of Jumu\'ah [Friday], then proceed to the remembrance of Allah and leave trade" (Qur\'an 62:9). Afterwards: "when the prayer has been concluded, disperse within the land and seek from the bounty of Allah, and remember Allah often" (Qur\'an 62:10).\n- Listen to the khutbah quietly.\n\nAsk me about the Friday prayer itself, who must attend, and how many rak\'ahs it has.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 854; Sahih al-Bukhari 881, 880; Qur\'an 62:9, 62:10.\n[GO:/prayer]',
