    answer: 'Tawheed is the belief that Allah is One in His being and in His right to be worshipped, with no partner. Allah says: "He is Allah, [who is] One, Allah, the Eternal Refuge. He neither begets nor is born, Nor is there to Him any equivalent" (Qur\'an 112:1-4).\n\nShirk is the opposite: giving someone or something else a share in what belongs to Allah alone, such as worshipping, praying to or relying completely on another besides Him. The Qur\'an treats it as the gravest wrong. Luqman told his son not to associate anything with Allah: "Indeed, association [with him] is great injustice" (Qur\'an 31:13). And "Indeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills" (Qur\'an 4:48). That verse is about dying while still committing it; the door of repentance stays open for a living person.\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ explained what Allah\'s right is: Mu\'adh reported the Prophet said Allah\'s right on His servants is that they worship Him alone and associate nothing with Him, and the servants\' right on Allah is that He does not punish the one who associates nothing with Him (Sahih al-Bukhari 2856).\n\nSource: Qur\'an 112:1-4, 31:13, 4:48; Sahih al-Bukhari 2856.\n[GO:/academy/aqeedah]',
