    answer: 'Between sunrise and sunset in Ramadan:\n- Intercourse breaks the fast, and doing it deliberately in the day of Ramadan is a major matter that requires a penalty (kaffarah) on top of making the day up. A man told the Prophet ﷺ he had been ruined for having relations with his wife while fasting; the Prophet ﷺ gave him the way of atonement: freeing a slave if he can, otherwise fasting two months in a row, otherwise feeding sixty poor people (Sahih al-Bukhari 1936). The Hanafi and Maliki schools put the same penalty on deliberate eating and drinking; the Shafi\'i and Hanbali schools apply it to intercourse only.\n- Kissing and embracing your spouse are allowed if you can control yourself. A\'ishah said the Prophet ﷺ used to kiss and embrace his wives while fasting, and that he had more power to control his desires than any of you (Sahih al-Bukhari 1927). If it leads you to go further, avoid it in the day.\n- Releasing semen on purpose (by hand or any other way) breaks the fast and needs a make-up day, and the person should repent; a wet dream does not break it.\n- The night is free: Allah allows relations with your wife from sunset until dawn (Qur\'an 2:187).\n\nIf the fast was broken by a slip, make up the day and ask Allah\'s forgiveness; ask a scholar if you are unsure which rule applies.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1936, 1927; Qur\'an 2:187.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-fasting]',
