    answer: 'Pork is forbidden for Muslims. Allah says: "He has only forbidden to you dead animals, blood, the flesh of swine, and that which has been dedicated to other than Allah" (Qur\'an 2:173). The same is said in Qur\'an 5:3 and Qur\'an 6:145. This covers the meat and fat (lard) of the pig and foods made from them, such as bacon, ham and pepperoni.\n\nPlease also check labels: gelatin, some enzymes, emulsifiers and shortening can come from pigs unless the label says halal, vegetable or beef. See the answer on gelatin.\n\nThe exception is necessity: the same verse says "whoever is forced [by necessity], neither desiring [it] nor transgressing [its limit], there is no sin upon him" (Qur\'an 2:173). If you eat it by mistake without knowing, there is no sin; just stop when you find out.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 2:173, 5:3, 6:145.',
