      r'\bsupermarket meat\b',
      r'\bmeat from (?:a )?(?:non muslim|christian|jewish|supermarket|restaurant)\b',
      r'\bnon muslim\b.*\b(?:meat|food|slaughter)\b',
      r'\b(?:meat|food)\b.*\b(?:people of the book|ahl al kitab|christians?|jews?)\b',
      r'\bbismillah\b.*\b(?:eat|meat|slaughter)\b',
      r'\bhalal (?:food|restaurant|restaurants|certification|certified)\b',
      r'\beat(?:ing)? (?:at|in) (?:a )?(?:non muslim|restaurant|mcdonalds|kfc|fast food)\b',
      r'\bwhat makes (?:meat|food) halal\b',
      r'\bhow (?:do|can|to) (?:i|we|you) (?:know|tell|check|find out) (?:if |whether )?(?:the )?(?:meat|food|chicken|beef|this|it) (?:is )?halal\b',
      r'\bhow to know (?:if )?(?:meat|food) is halal\b',
      r'\bis (?:kfc|mcdonalds|subway|fast food) halal\b',
      r'\bchicken\b.*\bhalal\b',
    ],
    avoid: <String>[
      r'\b(?:near me|nearby|app|find)\b',
    ],
    answer: 'Meat is halal when the animal is a permitted kind (cattle, sheep, goat, camel, chicken, deer, etc. - not pig, carnivores, or dead animals), and it is slaughtered properly: by a Muslim (or one of the People of the Book), with a sharp knife cutting the throat, saying "Bismillah, Allahu akbar" at the time, so that the blood flows. The Qur\'an forbids dead animals, blood, pork and what is dedicated to other than Allah (Qur\'an 5:3).\n\nWhat about meat from non-Muslims? The Qur\'an says "the food of those who were given the Scripture is lawful for you" (Qur\'an 5:5). The majority of scholars take this to mean the meat of Jews and Christians who slaughter in their religion\'s way is allowed. But many say today\'s industrial slaughter, which may not follow that, is not covered. So:\n- Safest: buy meat that is certified halal.\n- Kosher meat is accepted by many scholars as it follows a similar slaughter, though some require "Bismillah".\n- Supermarket or restaurant meat of unknown slaughter: scholars differ. Some allow it based on the verse above, citing the general rule that food is lawful unless known to be unlawful. Others say it is not allowed unless known to be halal. Following the stricter view is the common practice.\n- Stunning: allowed by many scholars if the animal is alive at the cut and would survive the stun; others reject it. Machine slaughter with a recorded "Bismillah" is also debated.\n- Fish and seafood do not need slaughter.\n\nIf you find yourself eating non-halal meat by mistake or when no halal exists, there is no sin on the one who does not know. Fast food chains differ by country and branch: check the certificate. The Masajid and Halal screen can help you find halal places.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 5:3, 5:5.\n[GO:/masajid]',
    topic: 'halal meat',
    beforeGate: true,
    reviewNote: 'Rulings on People of the Book meat, supermarket meat, stunning and machine slaughter are contested and described as differences; flagged for scholar review.',
  ),
  CoreEntry(
    id: 'tattoo',
    patterns: <String>[
      r'\btattoo\w*\b',
      r'\bpiercing\w*\b',
      r'\bear ?piercing\w*\b',
      r'\bnose ?piercing\w*\b',
      r'\bbody (?:art|modification)\b',
      r'\bpermanent makeup\b',
      r'\bmicroblading\b',
      r'\bhenna\b.*\b(?:halal|haram|allowed|sunnah)\b',
    ],
    avoid: <String>[
      r'\b(?:wudu|ghusl|prayer)\b',
    ],
    answer: 'Permanent tattoos are forbidden according to most scholars. The Prophet ﷺ said that Allah cursed the woman who tattoos and the one who has it done (Sahih al-Bukhari 5937). The reasons scholars give are that it changes Allah\'s creation, causes pain and harm, and blocks water in some views.\n\nPractical points:\n- If you got a tattoo before you were a Muslim, or before you knew, there is no sin on you now; repent and go forward. Wudu and prayer are valid with a tattoo.\n- Removing it: scholars say you are not required to remove a tattoo if removal would cause serious harm or great pain; remove it if that is easily done.\n- Henna and other temporary designs that wash off are allowed (for women and in moderation). Medical tattoos (for example, marking a radiation site or hiding a scar) are allowed by necessity.\n- Ear piercing for women is allowed; most scholars dislike or forbid body piercing for men that imitates women, and extreme body modification.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 5937.',
    topic: 'tattoo',
    beforeGate: true,
    reviewNote: 'Removal of old tattoos, piercings for men, and medical tattoos are standard fiqh positions; not text-checked here.',
  ),
  CoreEntry(
    id: 'dogs',
    patterns: <String>[
      r'\bdogs?\b',
      r'\bpuppy\b',
      r'\bpuppies\b',
      r'\bguide dogs?\b',
      r'\bservice dogs?\b',
