    ],
    answer: 'Cats: yes, you may keep them. The Prophet ﷺ said of the cat that it is not unclean (Sunan Abu Dawud 75, hasan sahih per al-Albani). He also warned that a woman entered the Fire because of a cat she had tied up and neither fed nor let go (Sahih al-Bukhari 3318). So caring for any animal is rewarded, and cruelty to one is a sin.\n\nOther pets (birds, fish, rabbits and so on) are allowed if you feed them, give them room and do not harm them. Do not keep a bird in a cage so small that it cannot live well. For dogs, ask me about dogs.\n\nSource: Sunan Abu Dawud 75, hasan sahih per al-Albani; Sahih al-Bukhari 3318.',
