    answer: 'For men, wearing gold and pure silk is forbidden; for women both are allowed. Abu Musa reported the Messenger of Allah said wearing silk and gold has been made unlawful for the males of my Ummah and lawful for its females (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 1720, sahih per Darussalam). He once pulled a gold ring from a man\'s hand and threw it away (Sahih Muslim 2090).\n\nSilver is allowed for men, and a silver ring was worn by the Prophet ﷺ (Sahih al-Bukhari 5865). Other metals such as platinum or steel, and silk mixed with other cloth, are allowed by most scholars; ask a scholar if you are unsure. A gold tooth filling or a gold nose or surgery fixture for medical need is allowed.\n\nSource: Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 1720, sahih per Darussalam; Sahih Muslim 2090; Sahih al-Bukhari 5865.',
