    avoid: <String>[
      r'\b(?:game|story)\b',
    ],
    answer: 'Allah tells believing women: "And tell the believing women to reduce [some] of their vision and guard their private parts and not expose their adornment except that which [necessarily] appears thereof and to wrap [a portion of] their headcovers over their chests" (Qur\'an 24:31). And in Qur\'an 33:59 He tells the Prophet to say to his wives, daughters and the believing women to bring down over themselves some of their outer garments.\n\nThe scholars agree that a woman covers her body in front of men who are not close relatives, and that men also have to cover from navel to knee and lower their gaze (Qur\'an 24:30). Most say the woman\'s face and hands may be uncovered, while some say the face too is covered (niqab); both views have scholars behind them. The hijab is a command in Islam, and a woman who is working up to it is still on the path.\n\nHijab is more than cloth: it is also modesty in behaviour, for men and women alike. Nobody should be forced into it or mocked for it; Allah says "There shall be no compulsion in [acceptance of] the religion" (Qur\'an 2:256).\n\nSource: Qur\'an 24:31, 33:59, 24:30, 2:256.',
