    answer: 'Smoking and vaping: most scholars today say they are forbidden, because they harm the body and Allah says "do not throw [yourselves] with your [own] hands into destruction" (Qur\'an 2:195) and "makes lawful for them the good things and prohibits for them the evil" (Qur\'an 7:157). Some older scholars called it only disliked, before the harm was known. Shisha and hookah are treated the same.\n\nDrugs that intoxicate, such as cannabis, cocaine and similar, are forbidden for the same reason as alcohol: see the answer on alcohol.\n\nIf you are trying to quit, that is a good intention and Allah rewards the effort. Ask a doctor for help, and remember that it breaks the fast (see the fasting answer).\n\nSource: Qur\'an 2:195, 7:157.',
