    answer: 'Marriage in Islam is a partnership with rights on both sides; the duties are not on one side only. Allah says "And due to the wives is similar to what is expected of them, according to what is reasonable" (Qur\'an 2:228), and calls the couple a source of "affection and mercy" (Qur\'an 30:21).\n\nFor the husband: to provide for his family, to treat his wife well and live with her in kindness (Qur\'an 4:19). Abu Hurairah narrated the Prophet said the most complete of the believers in faith is the one with the best character, and the best of you are those who are best to your women (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 1162, hasan sahih per al-Albani). And: The best of you is the one who is best to his wife, and I am the best of you to my wives (Sunan Ibn Majah 1977, hasan per Darussalam).\n\nFor the wife: to keep the trust of the marriage, to protect the home and herself in his absence, and, as the scholars explain, to cooperate with her husband in what is right (Qur\'an 4:34 describes righteous women as "devoutly obedient, guarding in [the husband\'s] absence what Allah would have them guard" (Qur\'an 4:34)). Both should be honest and loyal to each other.\n\nIf you disagree, speak calmly, forgive the small things (Qur\'an 4:19 says perhaps you dislike a thing and Allah makes therein much good), and ask family or a counsellor to help you, as in Qur\'an 4:35. Abu Huraira reported the Prophet said act kindly towards women, and a believing man should not hate a believing woman: if he dislikes one of her characteristics, he will be pleased with another (Sahih Muslim 1468).\n\nSource: Qur\'an 2:228, 30:21, 4:19, 4:34, 4:35; Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 1162, hasan sahih per al-Albani; Sunan Ibn Majah 1977, hasan per Darussalam; Sahih Muslim 1468.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-nikah]',
    topic: 'marriage',
    beforeGate: true,
    reviewNote: 'Description of the wife\'s duties follows the classical summary; the detail is a matter of fiqh and culture. Flagged for scholar review.',
  ),
  CoreEntry(
