      r'\bsuccessors? of the prophet\b',
    ],
    answer: 'The four Rightly Guided Caliphs (al-Khulafa ar-Rashidun) led the Muslim community after the Prophet ﷺ passed away in the year 11 AH (632 CE), in this order:\n1. Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (11-13 AH), the Prophet\'s close companion in the cave of the Hijrah (Qur\'an 9:40).\n2. Umar ibn al-Khattab (13-23 AH), who expanded the state and gathered the people behind one imam for Taraweeh.\n3. Uthman ibn Affan (23-35 AH), under whom the Qur\'an was copied into the standard written copies.\n4. Ali ibn Abi Talib (35-40 AH), cousin and son-in-law of the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nAll four were among the ten the Prophet ﷺ gave glad tidings of Paradise (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 3747, sahih per al-Albani). Sunni Muslims count these four as the Rightly Guided Caliphs; Shia Muslims hold a different view on the question of leadership after the Prophet ﷺ (see the answer on Sunni and Shia). This app does not rank Muslim groups.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 9:40; Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 3747, sahih per al-Albani.\n[GO:/stories]',
    topic: 'caliphs',
    beforeGate: true,
    reviewNote: 'Dates of the caliphates and the standard-copy detail are from standard history, not text-checked here. Flagged for scholar review. The Sunni/Shia sentence is deliberately neutral.',
  ),
  CoreEntry(
    id: 'companions-sahabah',
    patterns: <String>[
