      r'\bten companions\b',
    ],
    answer: 'A companion (sahabi) is a person who met the Prophet ﷺ, believed in him, and died as a Muslim. They learned Islam from him directly and passed it to us, and they are the best generation. Allah says: "And the first forerunners [in the faith] among the Muhajireen and the Ansar and those who followed them with good conduct - Allah is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him" (Qur\'an 9:100). Abdullah reported the Prophet said the best people are those living in my generation, and then those who will follow them, and then those who will follow the latter (Sahih al-Bukhari 3651).\n\nAmong them: the four Rightly Guided Caliphs (Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali); the ten given glad tidings of Paradise (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 3747, sahih per al-Albani); the Prophet\'s wives and daughters; and many Muhajirun and Ansar. Their stories are in the Stories section of this app.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 9:100; Sahih al-Bukhari 3651; Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 3747, sahih per al-Albani.\n[GO:/stories]',
