  CoreEntry(
    id: 'badr',
    patterns: <String>[
      r'\bbadr\b',
      r'\bbattle of badr\b',
      r'\bghazwat? badr\b',
      r'\bday of the criterion\b',
      r'\bfurqan\b.*\bbattle\b',
    ],
    answer: 'Badr was the first major battle between the Muslims of Madinah and the Quraysh of Makkah, fought in Ramadan in the year 2 AH. The Muslims were few and poorly armed, the Makkan army about three times as many, and Allah gave the believers victory: "And already had Allah given you victory at [the battle of] Badr while you were few in number" (Qur\'an 3:123).\n\nOn the numbers, Umar reported that on the day of Badr the Prophet cast a glance at the polytheists, who were one thousand, while his own companions were three hundred and nineteen, then turned towards the qiblah and made du\'a to his Lord (Sahih Muslim 1763). Al-Bara said that the Badr fighters were about three hundred and ten and some, like the companions of Talut (Sahih al-Bukhari 3959). Allah reminded them that He sent help with the angels (Qur\'an 8:9) and that victory is only from Him (Qur\'an 3:126).\n\nThe Qur\'an calls it the day of the Furqan (the Criterion), when truth was separated from falsehood. Those who fought at Badr are honoured among the companions.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 3:123, 8:9, 3:126; Sahih Muslim 1763; Sahih al-Bukhari 3959.',
    topic: 'badr',
    beforeGate: true,
    reviewNote: 'The date (Ramadan, 2 AH) and the "about three times" figure are from standard history and not text-checked here; the numbers cited are from the two hadith above.',
  ),
  CoreEntry(
    id: 'karbala',
    patterns: <String>[
      r'\bkarbala\b',
      r'\bkerbela\b',
      r'\bashura\b.*\b(?:husain|husayn|hussain|karbala)\b',
