    answer: 'The Qur\'an is the word of Allah, revealed to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ through the angel Jibreel (Qur\'an 2:97), in Arabic, in stages over about twenty-three years (the thirteen years in Makkah and ten in Madinah of Sahih al-Bukhari 3902). It began in the month of Ramadan: "The month of Ramadhan [is that] in which was revealed the Qur\'an, a guidance for the people" (Qur\'an 2:185), on the Night of Decree (Qur\'an 97:1).\n\nIt has 114 chapters (surahs), from Al-Fatihah to An-Nas. It is a guidance for belief, worship, character and daily life, and it is the central miracle of Islam. Allah promised to guard it: "Indeed, it is We who sent down the Qur\'an and indeed, We will be its guardian" (Qur\'an 15:9). It was memorised and written down during the Prophet\'s life, and Muslims have recited it by heart ever since, which is why the same text is read across the world.\n\nReading it, understanding it, and acting on it are all rewarded. You can read and hear it in the Qur\'an screen of this app, and the Hifz planner helps you memorise it.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 2:97, 2:185, 97:1, 15:9; Sahih al-Bukhari 3902.\n[GO:/quran]',
    topic: 'quran',
    beforeGate: true,
    reviewNote: 'Number of surahs is the commonly agreed 114; the "twenty-three years" follows from the cited hadith (13 plus 10).',
