    answer: 'The Ka\'bah is the cube-shaped House of Allah in the middle of the Sacred Mosque in Makkah. It is the direction (qiblah) that Muslims face in prayer: "So turn your face toward al-Masjid al-Haram. And wherever you [believers] are, turn your faces toward it [in prayer]" (Qur\'an 2:144).\n\nAllah says it was the first house of worship for mankind: "Indeed, the first House [of worship] established for mankind was that at Makkah - blessed and a guidance for the worlds" (Qur\'an 3:96). It was raised by Ibrahim and his son Ismail: "And [mention] when Abraham was raising the foundations of the House and [with him] Ishmael" (Qur\'an 2:127). Pilgrims circle it in the rite of tawaf during Hajj and Umrah, and Hajj to it is a duty for those who are able (Qur\'an 3:97).\n\nMuslims do not worship the Ka\'bah or the Black Stone set in its corner; they worship Allah alone. The Ka\'bah is a sign of unity: all Muslims in the world pray in its direction. The Qibla screen in this app shows the direction from where you are.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 2:144, 3:96, 2:127, 3:97.\n[GO:/qibla]',
