    answer: 'Allah is the Arabic name of the One God, Creator and Lord of everything, the same God worshipped by Ibrahim, Musa and Isa. The Qur\'an gives the simplest description in Surah Al-Ikhlas: "He is Allah, [who is] One" (Qur\'an 112:1), "Allah, the Eternal Refuge" (Qur\'an 112:2), "He neither begets nor is born" (Qur\'an 112:3), "Nor is there to Him any equivalent" (Qur\'an 112:4).\n\nSome of what He tells us about Himself:\n- "There is nothing like unto Him, and He is the Hearing, the Seeing" (Qur\'an 42:11): nothing in creation resembles Him.\n- "He is Allah, other than whom there is no deity, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed. He is the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful" (Qur\'an 59:22).\n- "Allah - there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of [all] existence. Neither drowsiness overtakes Him nor sleep." (Qur\'an 2:255)\n\nThis oneness (tawhid) is the heart of Islam. Worshipping anything with Him is shirk: "Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills" (Qur\'an 4:48). Muslims know Him through His Names; the 99 Names game and screen in this app teach them.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 112:1, 112:2, 112:3, 112:4, 42:11, 59:22, 2:255, 4:48.\n[GO:/games/names99]',
