    avoid: <String>[
      r'\b(?:game|story|stories|angel investor)\b',
    ],
    answer: 'Angels are creatures of Allah, made from light, who obey Him and do what they are told: "angels, harsh and severe; they do not disobey Allah in what He commands them but do what they are commanded" (Qur\'an 66:6). A\'isha reported the Prophet said the angels were created from light, the jinn from the spark of fire, and Adam from what has been described to you (Sahih Muslim 2996). They are not male or female, and not partners with Allah.\n\nJibreel (Gabriel) is the angel of revelation who brought the Qur\'an to the Prophet ﷺ: "Whoever is an enemy to Gabriel - it is [none but] he who has brought the Qur\'an down upon your heart" (Qur\'an 2:97). He also came in the form of a man to teach the Companions their religion, asking about Islam, iman and ihsan (Sahih Muslim 8). Mikail (Michael) is named in Qur\'an 2:98.\n\nOther angels do other tasks: recording deeds, protecting, taking souls, and guarding Paradise and the Fire. The Qur\'an and hadith do not give details of every one, so the guidance is to believe in what is told and not to guess beyond it. Belief in the angels is the second article of iman.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 66:6, 2:97, 2:98; Sahih Muslim 2996, 8.',
