      r'\bfuneral\b',
    ],
    answer: 'Muslims believe that death is not the end but the move to the next stage. Here is what the Qur\'an and hadith tell us.\n\n- Death: the soul is taken, and the person enters the barzakh, a barrier between this life and the Day of Resurrection. The Qur\'an says of those who wish to return: "No! It is only a word he is saying; and behind them is a barrier until the Day they are resurrected" (Qur\'an 23:100).\n- Resurrection: all people will be raised, and each will be reckoned. "And We place the scales of justice for the Day of Resurrection, so no soul will be treated unjustly at all. And if there is [even] the weight of a mustard seed, We will bring it forth." (Qur\'an 21:47)\n- Accountability: "So whoever does an atom\'s weight of good will see it, And whoever does an atom\'s weight of evil will see it." (Qur\'an 99:7-8)\n- Then Paradise (Jannah) for the believers and the Fire (Jahannam) for those who reject and do wrong, subject to Allah\'s mercy and justice. Belief in the Last Day is the fifth article of iman (Sahih Muslim 8).\n\nDetails such as the questioning in the grave and the bridge are reported in authentic hadith but are matters of the unseen, so we believe in what is told and do not argue about how. Allah is the Most Merciful: "do not despair of the mercy of Allah" (Qur\'an 39:53).\n\nSource: Qur\'an 23:100, 21:47, 99:7-8, 39:53; Sahih Muslim 8.\n[GO:/academy/aqeedah]',
